; Consumers take this package as a Git dependency. pnpm prepares a git-hosted
; package by invoking the npm CLI in this directory: it ignores the
; packageManager field, and it strips npm_config_* from the child environment,
; so this file is the only place the setting below can be applied.
;
; npm 10's peer resolver crashes on the vitest 4.1.x dependency graph with
; "Cannot read properties of null (reading 'edgesOut')". That aborts the
; prepare step, so every consumer on Node 22 fails to resolve this package.
; npm 11 (Node 24) is unaffected, as is vitest 4.0.18 and earlier.
;
; Scope: only a package manager whose cwd is THIS directory reads it, so the
; repository-root workspace install is unaffected. Drop this file once the
; npm 10 line is no longer a consumer's default.
legacy-peer-deps=true
